preConditionHook:
// SwingTrailCappedAtMaxRisk -- Grimes A list (G08-21, key
// SwingTrailCappedAtMaxRisk; also G08-09, key SwingPointTrailingStopAtRank, as
// pivotIndex). Authored 2026-09-22 as new inputs on SwingPointTrailingStop and
// split out 2026-11-07, because the 202611 BRK and OWN templates place
// SwingPointTrailingStop, so that rule stays exactly as those families run it.
// Code otherwise unchanged.
//
// DEFAULTS: maxRiskAtr(2) is Grimes's "about 2 ATR", the merged candidate's
// value; pivotIndex(1) trails the most recent pivot; the other inputs are
// SwingPointTrailingStop's. At maxRiskAtr 0 the cap is off, and at pivotIndex 1
// with maxRiskAtr 0 this is SwingPointTrailingStop's behaviour exactly.
//
// GUARD (2026-09-17): a level's EXISTENCE is a COUNT of pivots the scan found,
// never a test of the price against -1 -- a back-adjusted series can print
// -1.00 (or 0.00) as a real price. The EL twin counts the same way. Mentions of
// the -1 SENTINEL below describe what EL's SwingLow / SwingHigh return, not how
// this rule guards it.
// THE HEADLINE BROOKS TRAIL. While long, the protective stop sits just below the
// pivotIndex-th most recent CONFIRMED swing low and moves with each new pivot;
// mirrored above the swing high while short. Nine mined candidates from all
// three volumes collapse into this one rule.
//
// Not TrailingStop / AtrTrailingStop, which trail a dollar or ATR distance below
// the position's PEAK PROFIT: on a trend that pauses the dollar trail tightens
// with every new high while this one does not move until a new pivot confirms.
// Not StopBeyondRecentRangeExtreme, whose level is an N-bar lowest low taken
// through the previous bar -- a Donchian floor that moves every bar the window
// rolls, where a pivot is a chart structure that only changes when one forms.
// Not SwingPivotTarget, which is a profit target at the OPPOSING pivot (a long
// exits at the swing high); this is a stop at the SAME-side pivot. Not
// InitialStopBeyondSwingAtEntry, which freezes the pivot that existed at entry.
//
// FOUR SOURCES ADD "only after the market makes a new high", which is dropped as
// redundant: a fresh swing low only becomes the most recent one after a rally, so
// the trigger adds no bars and would cost a Highest() call site.
//
// THE LEVEL IS READ FRESH EVERY BAR AND IS NOT RATCHETED. Brooks phrases it as
// "raise the stop", but the merged pseudocode is the plain read, and a per
// position monotone ratchet is exactly the machinery TrailStopBehindStrongBar and
// StopBeyondExtremeSinceEntry already carry -- adding it here would make this the
// same machine at a different reference and would need an at-entry seed the
// sources do not give. A deeper pullback that prints a LOWER swing low therefore
// widens the stop; maxRiskAtr below is the only bound on that.
//
// TWO GRIMES READINGS, one rule.
//
// (1) pivotIndex (G08-09, key SwingPointTrailingStopAtRank). "In an uptrend a
// tight stop could be trailed under the highest pivot low of the trend; slightly
// wider stops could go under the second-highest, probably working both on a
// close-only basis." The highest pivot low of an uptrend IS the most recent one,
// so RANK is the only new degree of freedom, and SwingPointTrailingStop was
// already close-only. At pivotIndex 1, the default, the pivot is
// SwingPointTrailingStop's. THE SCAN IS THE THREE-PIVOT FORM SwingPivotTarget
// ALREADY CARRIES, because the register lists SwingLow / SwingHigh Occurrence 3+
// as UNMEASURED -- the deeper ranks are found by hand, pivotIndex is CLAMPED to
// the three pivots kept, and there is no early break, so the scan can reach
// them. The equivalence at pivotIndex 1 is BEHAVIOURAL, not textual: the first
// pivot found scanning newest-first is the same bar SwingPointTrailingStop's
// scan, which breaks at the first pivot, returns; the EL twin spells the same
// hand-rolled scan and its pivot count where SwingPointTrailingStop calls
// SwingLow(1, ...) / SwingLowBar(1, ...).
//
// (2) maxRiskAtr and atrLength (G08-21, key SwingTrailCappedAtMaxRisk). A HARD
// FLOOR AT THE INITIAL RISK: the long stop becomes the HIGHER of (the pivot less
// the offset) and (EntryPrice - maxRiskAtr ATRs), so the trail may widen to
// emerging structure but never past 1R; the short is the mirror LOWER of the two.
// maxRiskAtr 0 MEANS UNBOUNDED, not "a floor at the entry price": at 0 the cap
// is off and the trail is SwingPointTrailingStop's, and a floor at EntryPrice
// would be a breakeven stop, a different rule. The engine has no initial-risk accessor, so
// the cap is stated in ATRs rather than in the stop placement's own distance --
// the SwingPivotTarget substitution. Grimes's value is about 2 ATR.
// MaxList IS DELIBERATELY NOT USED: the register's maxlist / minlist row is
// ACCEPTED only for selection among TICK-GRID PRICE operands, and
// EntryPrice - maxRiskAtr * ATR is a COMPUTED operand whose tolerance behaviour
// is unmeasured. An explicit comparison is plain EL and carries the measured
// relational tolerance, so el_gt mirrors it exactly.
// THE PIVOT GUARD STILL LEADS: with no pivot in the window the rule does not
// fire at all, cap or no cap, exactly as SwingPointTrailingStop behaves.
// EntryPrice is 0.0 while flat (VERIFIED), so the level is only trusted behind
// the MarketPosition guard in the conditions.
//
// THE PIVOT SCAN IS INLINED from SwingHigh per the B-list decision. MEASURED
// (EL_Swing_Probe.txt / el_swing_output1.txt, @ES 60 min): the pivot test is
// MIXED -- at-or-beyond the pivotStrength OLDER bars, STRICTLY beyond the
// pivotStrength NEWER bars, and bars-ago indexing makes the SMALLER index the
// NEWER bar, so the strict half is the kk < jj loop; the confirmation lag is
// exactly pivotStrength bars, never 0 or 1, so the level is knowable without
// lookahead and during the lag the PREVIOUS pivot is reported; lookbackBars is
// EL's Length, offsets 0..lookbackBars-1 inclusive, and the neighbourhood test
// reaches pivotStrength bars PAST the window, so the deepest pivot bar touched is
// lookbackBars - 1 + pivotStrength; an empty window returns the -1 SENTINEL,
// guarded by the pivot counts because -1 as a PRICE sits under every real price
// and would take every long off; the comparisons carry the 2.22e-12 relational
// tolerance, hence el_lt / el_le / el_gt / el_ge. The low side's tie sense is the
// mirror of the measured high-side rule. No WFSafe_SwingLow exists, so plain EL
// governs. The scan runs unconditionally every bar, so Max Bars Back covers it
// and the EasyLanguage twin advances on the same bars.
//
// WFSafe_AvgTrueRange is MultiWalk's ROLLING accumulator, not the built-in it
// resembles: seeded with a full N-term sum on the first calculated bar and again
// whenever the length changes, thereafter updated as TWO statements -- EL
// evaluates S[1] + in - out left to right and folding it to S += in - out rounds
// differently. Ported from AtrProfitTarget / SwingPivotTarget, read once per bar
// into a local (EL does not short-circuit and/or). The local counter is atrLen,
// not atrLength: atrLength is this rule's INPUT.
//
// lookbackBars is not in the merged parameter list and is what makes the pivot
// window addressable; 40 is the corpus default (SwingPivotTarget,
// ShrinkingSwingIncrementsExit). Offsets are one tick everywhere in the sources,
// and the tick is written division-first, trailOffsetTicks * (ctx.MinMove() /
// ctx.PriceScale()), read once per bar into a local since MinMove and PriceScale
// are per-symbol constants for the whole run.
//
// Every scratch value is a localVariables entry, never a hook-scope declaration,
// so the hooks survive a double placement.
//
// Deepest bar touched: max(lookbackBars - 1 + pivotStrength, atrLength + 1).
tickSize = ctx.MinMove() / ctx.PriceScale();
if (atrLen != (int)atrLength) {
    atrSum = 0.0;
    for (int i = 0; i < (int)atrLength; ++i) {
        double hi = high[i] > close[i + 1] ? high[i] : close[i + 1];
        double lo = low[i] < close[i + 1] ? low[i] : close[i + 1];
        atrSum += hi - lo;
    }
    atrLen = (int)atrLength;
} else {
    const int out = (int)atrLength;
    double hiIn = high[0] > close[1] ? high[0] : close[1];
    double loIn = low[0] < close[1] ? low[0] : close[1];
    double hiOut = high[out] > close[out + 1] ? high[out] : close[out + 1];
    double loOut = low[out] < close[out + 1] ? low[out] : close[out + 1];
    atrSum += hiIn - loIn;
    atrSum -= hiOut - loOut;
}
atrVal = atrSum / (int)atrLength;
nHiPiv = 0;
nLoPiv = 0;
hiPx1 = -1.0;
hiPx2 = -1.0;
hiPx3 = -1.0;
loPx1 = -1.0;
loPx2 = -1.0;
loPx3 = -1.0;
for (jj = (int)pivotStrength; jj <= (int)lookbackBars - 1; ++jj) {
    okHi = true;
    okLo = true;
    for (kk = jj - (int)pivotStrength; kk < jj; ++kk) {
        if (!el_gt(high[jj], high[kk])) okHi = false;
        if (!el_lt(low[jj], low[kk])) okLo = false;
    }
    for (kk = jj + 1; kk <= jj + (int)pivotStrength; ++kk) {
        if (!el_ge(high[jj], high[kk])) okHi = false;
        if (!el_le(low[jj], low[kk])) okLo = false;
    }
    if (okHi && nHiPiv < 3) {
        nHiPiv = nHiPiv + 1;
        if (nHiPiv == 1) hiPx1 = high[jj];
        if (nHiPiv == 2) hiPx2 = high[jj];
        if (nHiPiv == 3) hiPx3 = high[jj];
    }
    if (okLo && nLoPiv < 3) {
        nLoPiv = nLoPiv + 1;
        if (nLoPiv == 1) loPx1 = low[jj];
        if (nLoPiv == 2) loPx2 = low[jj];
        if (nLoPiv == 3) loPx3 = low[jj];
    }
}
needP = (int)pivotIndex;
if (needP < 1) needP = 1;
if (needP > 3) needP = 3;
hi1 = hiPx3;
lo1 = loPx3;
if (needP == 1) { hi1 = hiPx1; lo1 = loPx1; }
if (needP == 2) { hi1 = hiPx2; lo1 = loPx2; }
haveLo1 = (nLoPiv >= needP);
haveHi1 = (nHiPiv >= needP);
stopLevelLong = lo1 - trailOffsetTicks * tickSize;
stopLevelShort = hi1 + trailOffsetTicks * tickSize;
if (el_gt(maxRiskAtr, 0.0)) {
    riskFloor = ctx.EntryPrice() - maxRiskAtr * atrVal;
    if (el_gt(riskFloor, stopLevelLong)) stopLevelLong = riskFloor;
    riskFloor = ctx.EntryPrice() + maxRiskAtr * atrVal;
    if (el_lt(riskFloor, stopLevelShort)) stopLevelShort = riskFloor;
}
